## 6. WebSocket Events & Messaging Protocol

All real-time actions are managed through Socket.IO events defined in `packages/shared`:

| Event Name | Direction | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `room:join` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Join a watchroom with participant credentials |
| `room:leave` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Leave a watchroom |
| `room:state` | Server $\rightarrow$ Client | Broadcast full room state (`RoomState`) to room |
| `playback:play` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Resume playback at specified position |
| `playback:pause` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Pause playback at specified position |
| `playback:seek` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Seek to specific position |
| `playback:load` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Load a specific YouTube video |
| `playback:next` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Skip to next track in queue |
| `playback:ended` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Signal that current video finished |
| `queue:add` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Add video to queue |
| `queue:remove` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Remove item from queue |
| `queue:reorder` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Reorder queue items |
| `room:user-remove` | Client $\rightarrow$ Server | Kick/remove a user from the room |
| `room:user-kicked` | Server $\rightarrow$ Client | Notify target user that they were removed |
| `room:chat-message` | Bi-directional | Broadcast new chat message |
| `room:chat-reaction` | Bi-directional | Toggle emoji reaction on message |
| `room:chat-delete` | Bi-directional | Un-send / delete a chat message |
| `room:chat-edit` | Bi-directional | Edit a chat message within 2 minutes |

